Day 040 - BMI Calculator

What I practiced

Creating a function that calculates Body Mass Index (BMI) using weight and height.

What I learned

* Functions can accept multiple parameters.
* The return keyword sends a calculated result back.
* BMI is calculated using this formula:

BMI = weight (kg) / height (m)²

* The ** operator raises a number to a power.
* We can use if/else if/else to categorize a result.

Example

function calculateBMI(weight, height) {
    return weight / (height ** 2);
}
const bmi = calculateBMI(70, 1.85);
console.log("BMI:", bmi.toFixed(2));

Expected output

BMI: 20.45

Run

node day-040/script.js
